{
  "text": "2013A14 Briefly\ndescribe the structure of mitochondria.\nOutline the metabolic processes that occur in mitochondria.\nList:\n·\nIntro\n·\nStructure\n·\nFunctions\n·\nIllustrations\nIntro:\n·\nIntracellular organelle\n·\nFor energy production\n·\nAbundant in metabolically active tissue\n·\nAbsent in few cells e.g. RBC\n·\nOwn DNA, maternal inheritance\nStructure:\nFunctions:\nMetabolic\n·\nOxidative phosphorylation (inner membrane)\no\n36 mol\n  ATP per molecule of glucose\n·\nCitric acid cycle (matrix)\n·\nβ-oxidation of fatty acids (matrix)\nOther\n·\nThermogenesis\no\nUncoupling\n  protein inserted into inner membrane\no\nPassage\n  of H\n+\nwithout ATP formation\no\nOnly in\n  brown fat\no\nActivated\n  by adrenaline at β\n3\nreceptor\n·\nApoptosis\n·\nCalcium sequestration\n·\nDrug biotransformation\nPathway\nillustration:\nOxidative phosphorylation\nElectron transport chain rap:\n((\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VER6xW_r1vc\n)\nTCA cycle\nβ\n-oxidation\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
